  "stctt.w.cond.ucetc": "Prop. 3",
  "stctt.w.v.add": "<b>No transfer pays at λ = {l}.</b> In every coalition each carrier ships alone, C(N) = Σ C({i}) = {cn}, the game is additive, and its only core allocation is the stand-alone costs ({u}).",
  "stctt.w.v.add.utc": "Proposition 2 covers this case (λ &gt; {th}); with these data transfers stop paying already from λ = {c}.",
  "stctt.w.v.add.pre": "Proposition 2 does not apply yet (it needs λ &gt; {th}): with these data transfers stop paying from λ = {c}, long before the sufficient condition holds.",
  "stctt.w.v.empty": "<b>The core is empty.</b> Each carrier must pay at least its floor C(N) − C(N \\ {i}), or the other two would leave: {b} = {sb} &gt; C(N) = {cn}. Collaboration saves {sav}, yet no split keeps every group, the argument of Example 3. The split closest to stable still charges some coalition {e} more than it would pay alone.",
  "stctt.w.v.ok": "<b>The core is non-empty.</b> Collaboration saves {sav}, and the LP finds a split in which every coalition pays at least {e} less than on its own.",
  "stctt.w.v.ok0": "<b>The core is non-empty, with margin 0.</b> Collaboration saves {sav}, but in every core allocation some coalition pays exactly what it would pay on its own.",
  "stctt.w.v.nf": "No fixed transfer costs (Proposition 1): the game is a linear production game, and the dual (4) gives the Owen allocation u = ({u}), shown in the tables. Price per unit shipped η = ({eta}); capacity discounts {gam}. The dual value {z} equals C(N).",
  "stctt.w.v.gam": "γ = {v} for carrier {i} on leg {p}",
